        "original_id": "eb47dac8-1e3a-5f3d-9b1e-50060c72c218",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: Cadillac insurance plan\n- Events: Clinton health care plan debate\n- People: Bill Clinton\n- Roles: chair of the task force\n- Topics: United States medical-cost control measures, 1993 healthcare reform\n\nFacts:\n- In the early 1990s, the term Cadillac insurance plan gained popularity during United States debates over medical-cost control measures.\n- A Cadillac insurance plan is an unusually expensive health insurance plan.\n- In 1993, the Clinton health care plan was a healthcare reform package proposed by the administration of President Bill Clinton.\n- The Clinton health care plan was closely associated with the chair of the task force that devised the plan.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
